# Keys whose signature on an approve/<head-sha> tag counts as the owner's approval of a pull request (ADR-0005,
# slice 3 step B; scripts/signed-approval.mjs, .github/workflows/human-approval.yml). Git's allowed-signers format, one
# key per line:   <email> namespaces="git" <key-type> <public-key> [comment]
# Only hardware-backed key types count (sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com, sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com), so a
# signature needs a physical touch the agent cannot give. The checks read this file as main has it, never a branch's
# copy, so adding a key takes a merged pull request. No key is listed yet: until one is, signed approval is N/A.
